_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Uq06r","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-23T14:11:44Z","updated_at":"2025-11-23T14:11:44Z","body":"If you ignore the `.uid` file sure, but that assumes the file wasn't renamed, or that there isn't other files with the same name in the project that already took the same UID (even after fixing this PR to make it not generate duplicates)\r\n\r\nHaving two files with the same name in a project would be pretty likely depending on the name, so in all those cases this wouldn't fix anything (it also wouldn't work for any existing UID, those would be different in this case)\r\n\r\nI'd say the better solution for this edge case is handling those directly using the UID cache to recover orphan files, this has already been discussed in other contexts","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3567996587/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perform